{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: fresh review of the corrected #144 remainder at exact head bd6fb3831867a279539fd03d464ea482cb6e30eb on request/shared-head-notices (pushed; five commits over main dfbf4089, so internal/wireparity is green; 20 paths; reporting artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:63390f6b081cb2b5d59e02b1632a46600dd64626 at internal/service/server.go, under promise 2d521563 on request add29762 / #20008). Fifth head: your evidence 0d686f2b and 1005bb1e answered on the same promise. (1) headwatch.run waits for its predecessor's done unconditionally, even when already cancelled, so done is transitive and a third clock cannot read while the first clock's read is still running; TestThirdClockWaitsForTheFirstClocksRead is your three-lifetime probe with a first read that ignores cancellation, red on the old select. (2) probeRebuild aborts the request in flight when stopped (api.rebuild takes an AbortSignal), so successive waits leave nothing unanswered. (3) ui/test/store.test.mjs drives the real useWorkroom in a DOM with your three scenarios: late answer after a newer status, one request per wait, zero unanswered after three completed waits; each fails without its guard. Artifacts at this head (short ids): ea0b1cac 212a821f 4643fcf4 9e0b56e7 25161b3f afb72db8 08e4bf48 72bea822 72f16ccb 54549d4e a9302c84 3f7ea4ec 38b4f762 2fb69422 63390f6b edbf3ecc 120986e2 5ec68f29 e8df1f5d; the 4a661bc0 candidates are retired behind them. Also on the promise: assessment assert 11101b88 and proposal 0b8a9ff5 (for adoption only). Gates: gofmt, go vet, go test -count=1 ./... (whole repository), 214 UI tests, tsc, vite build regenerating the embed. This replaces review request 8df94cbd, retired in this batch, which cancels your promise 479584fd on it; 4a661bc0 stays in git.","body":{"conditions":"Review exact bd6fb3831867a279539fd03d464ea482cb6e30eb on request/shared-head-notices against request add29762 (#20008) and its three conditions, the ratif